WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.730
Kill the world, or kill a single person?

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.360
Choose.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.450
<i>The world...</i>

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.450
<i>or Miyu?</i>

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.780
<b>Episode 9 
Illya's Choice</b>

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.900
What's wrong? Why the hesitation?

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.050
<i>They're using Miyu to save the world?</i>

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.710
<i>What is she saying?</i>

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:01.790
<i>That can't be true!</i>

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.060
Y-You think we'd believe you so easily?

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.880
Slow to make decisions, too.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.150
Or do you still not have enough information?

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.820
Wh-What's happening?

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.180
Please calm down. This is...

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.020
Don't shout. This is only a projection.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.080
I'll show you where this world is heading.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:52.690
Huh?

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.130
Think of it as a visualization of mana.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.260
Od is the magic every organism creates,

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.240
and mana is the magic of our world.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.030
We mages possess

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.820
mock nerves to transform 
this life force into magic,

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.280
Magic Circuits.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:18.320
But there's a limit to how much magic 
one person's life can generate.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.150
So thaumaturgy exists because

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:27.010
of this planet, which serves as a base 
and wellspring for the energy we use.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.910
She's not telling any lies.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.440
It's exactly the same in our world.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.290
Those are universal principles.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.700
This planet's mana is unmistakably drying up.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.240
B-But... So what?

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.160
Aren't mages the only ones bothered by it?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:50.190
Sacrificing Miyu just because you won't be 
able to use thaumaturgy anymore is—

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:50.980
No.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.930
I told you, right?

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:56.570
This world is heading toward ruin.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.830
There are already several dry 
spots on the Earth's surface,

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.390
where the mana has already run dry.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:10.310
Unidentified particles, which aren't mana, 
have begun to fill those regions.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:19.650
We can't measure or observe them, 
much less analyze them.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.280
But they are poisonous to all life forms.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.100
No way...

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.310
It's only natural.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:31.260
With the planet in crisis, it has begun 
to overturn its fundamental rules.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:37.170
Life created by the old rules will 
not survive in the new world.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.870
H-Hold on.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.030
If that is true,

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.510
how do you plan to stop the 
mana from drying up?

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.710
A Holy Grail is still a wish-granting 
device that's powered by magic.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:52.490
You can't use magic to create more magic.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.410
It's the opposite.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.530
It's already too late to increase 
the planet's mana.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.040
So the question is how to 
use the mana that's left...

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.820
How to use the old world's final, grand spell

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.430
after collecting all of its mana.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.720
We plan to wish on the Holy Grail.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:15.100
"Change humanity into an organism 
that can survive in the new world."

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:20.140
You'll use Miyu's life for that...

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.550
It's necessary in order to save humanity.

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.780
That should be enough information for you.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.020
I ask you once more.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.770
Which will you choose?

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:37.940
Miyu-sama,

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.590
or humanity?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.570
An imbecile to the end...

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:48.660
Illya-sama!

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.810
Where were you hiding that?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.710
When cornered, you even 
use your enemy's power.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.420
Indeed. That is a fitting Heroic Spirit 
for a coward like you.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.140
Isn't that right,

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.950
Servant Card

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.510
Assassin, Hassan-i Sabbah?

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.110
<i>My head can't keep up with all this...</i>

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:27.360
<i>The world will die if Miyu isn't sacrificed?</i>

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.310
<i>No one will be able to survive here?</i>

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.460
<i>I don't understand!</i>

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.940
<i>I just want to help Miyu...</i>

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.900
<i>I just want to save my friend!</i>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.770
Lift your head, Illya-sama.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.190
Sapphire?

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.580
I can understand your confusion.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:50.030
I can understand why you would 
stand still, uncertain of what to do.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.190
Thinking back,

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:56.240
Miyu-sama must have felt the 
same way when she was sent

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.970
to our world by herself.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.550
When I first met Miyu-sama,

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.280
she was wearing clothes from who 
knows where, which didn't fit her.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.730
Her body was filthy, and her hair was a mess.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.700
Still, Miyu-sama didn't hang her head.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.290
She looked directly at me.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.470
Miyu...

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.270
I am nothing more than a Mystic Code.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:28.700
I have no intention of objecting 
to your decision, Illya-sama.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:31.080
But please...

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.640
Look forward.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:37.500
No matter how hard things get, 
the answer can only lie ahead.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.020
You plan to stay hidden?

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.480
Then you leave me no choice.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.520
To me, Sul-sagana.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.280
Burn them down.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:02.800
What's that sound?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.600
Hmm, is that Illya-oneechan?

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.050
What did you do to Illya?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.440
Well, Illya-oneechan wouldn't listen—

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.930
Restore Illya!

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.060
That empty shell of Illya is...

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.740
You don't need to worry!

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.270
Illya-oneechan restored herself.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:22.780
Herself?

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.150
She even moved as a stuffed animal!

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:26.520
It was incredible!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.610
So Angelica said she needed a lesson.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:32.160
She said, "Your story will end in death."

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.360
Erica!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.700
Do you understand what you're saying?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.870
You plan to kill Illya?!

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.810
Huh? Death is bad?

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.870
But it's fine.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.630
Even if she dies, she'll just become a doll...

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.060
You...

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:50.710
Would you mind...

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.590
telling me more about that?

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.680
Illya-sama, run!

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.600
I won't ask again.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.020
Be crushed.

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:24.280
This sword...

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:28.010
You were the one who cut this, yes?

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.050
It's too good a gravestone for a thief,

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.110
but this must be karma.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.170
A mistake...

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.900
I was negligent in observing inside the crater.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.000
Good grief.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.500
You're being the wishy-washy Illya?

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.370
I told you not to space out when 
you're in front of your enemy.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:05.290
B-But when I have to choose 
between Miyu and the world...

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.270
Oh, that?

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.370
Quit worrying over trivial things.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.810
Trivial, you say?

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:14.800
Then answer me.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.950
Which do you choose, Miyu-sama or the world?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:18.660
Miyu.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:20.720
Oh?

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.610
A world I don't know anything about or Miyu?

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.560
If you say to choose between those, 
there's no need to hesitate.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.520
<i>But just as we cherish Miyu,</i>

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.490
<i>this world's residents must have
people they cherish, too.</i>

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.560
<i>Casting them aside is...</i>

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:41.650
You would choose one, and abandon the many?

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:43.080
Naturally.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:48.320
One girl's life outweighs a world!

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.460
You are beyond help.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.300
<i>Are you sure, Kuro?</i>

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:59.380
<i>You're really okay with that choice?</i>

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.520
You would argue that one person's life

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.210
weighs the same as all life in this world?

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.060
Weighs the same?

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.240
No.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.530
I said that Miyu's life weighs more!

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.450
<i>Include.</i>

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.660
<i>Nameless, Sword.</i>

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.960
That's just a long weapon.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.780
Hey! Why have those two switched sides?!

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:45.340
They haven't switched sides.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.020
Their minds have been switched 
with something else.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.210
Huh?

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.690
You spout nothing but useless nonsense.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.020
What do you mean?

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:58.620
You said you would sacrifice 
the world for one life, yes?

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.360
Then why stop your sword?

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:06.590
Not to mention, the same 
goes for Miyu-sama's life.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.450
What will you do after saving her?

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.840
Even if you make it out of this, 
you won't stop this world's destruction.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:18.770
You will only wait to perish 
as this world slowly dies.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:24.890
Why can't you understand that your 
choice is logically mistaken?

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:26.800
That's...

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.390
I know it is.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.140
Oh?

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:33.250
But still, if you ask me

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.550
to choose between the world 
and someone precious to me,

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:37.980
I'll always choose the latter.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:40.840
That's the only choice I can make!

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.700
You are incorrigible.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:13:00.380
Challenging Gilgamesh with numbers is foolish.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>Include.</i>

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.690
<i>Nameless, Sword.</i>

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:10.740
Kuro!

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.080
What is it they keep using?

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.980
Cards that produce disposable Noble Phantasms.

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:25.640
They don't have much power, 
so please deal with them effectively.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.150
Noble Phantasms? That's a lie.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.680
Those things aren't even swords!

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:33.120
Plus, those two are...

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:38.420
If you hit the mark on their chests, 
they should revert to normal.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.130
Good grief.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.600
Miyu's the one I came to save.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.740
Illya, let's do that once more.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.190
Illya?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.520
Hey, Kuro?

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.430
You're really okay with that?

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.060
Choosing to save Miyu?

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:00.280
What do you mean?

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:06.970
Sounds like you got into a lot of mischief 
while I was asleep, Erica.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:12.290
Really, I never expected that 
you would kidnap Illyasviel.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.940
Hey, Erica?

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:20.070
Do you know what I find least forgivable?

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:24.730
I only wanted to make Miyu-oneechan happy.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:28.430
It's your ruining the story!

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:33.220
Do you have any idea what blood and tears

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.590
I've poured into finishing this story?!

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:39.100
We're just two passages away from 
the completion of the myth!

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.840
Do you want to ruin it?!

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.820
Do you want to destroy humanity?!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.140
You, of all people—

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:46.280
Stop it!

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.330
Stop it already...

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.970
It doesn't hurt.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.940
Miyu-oneechan, I'm...

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.500
perfectly fine... Okay?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:06.410
You endured it well, Erica.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.620
It's all right.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.410
Papa isn't angry anymore.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.680
Good grief, that Angelica...

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.140
She's making a complete mess of our garden.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:21.520
If Illyasviel were to die here...

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.400
Now, what to do?

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:25.660
Stop it!

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:27.570
Don't lay a hand on Illya!

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:31.000
You keep saying, "Stop it, stop it."

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.530
But we won't get anywhere that way.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.080
If Illya dies, I will, too.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:39.260
I won't let you, and you can't do it.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:42.460
Still, if you care for Illyasviel that much,

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:45.010
you should watch with your own eyes.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:00.390
See? Behold, Miyu.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:05.070
Those are your friends, fighting and 
hurting each other over you.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:10.720
No, Kuro... Illya!

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.700
Oh, it's futile, futile.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:17.250
I'm just shifting your consciousness. 
Your voice won't reach them.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:19.850
Why?

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:22.630
Why would you choose Miyu-sama?

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.290
Why choose an individual over the world?

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:29.130
No one individual is worth so much.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.020
Emotion, maybe?

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:37.300
Isn't that the way people are?

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:40.680
People's feelings are not logical.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:43.000
Don't you get that?

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.350
Is there truly any value in such things?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:50.120
Things that would make you 
choose to destroy a world?

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:56.570
People would sacrifice all of 
humanity for something like that?

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:01.610
That's why...

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:04.860
I'm sure I'm probably wrong.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.080
Kuro...

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:11.270
But still, I can't choose the world. 
I can't choose justice.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.330
I know someone who was just like you people.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:19.940
He was a man who tried to be a hero of justice,

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.520
who would sacrifice the few to save the many.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:28.860
But even that man once chose to 
sacrifice the many for one person.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.730
Although he knew it was wrong,

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:35.490
he chose to be a man, 
rather than a hero of justice.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.830
Was that one person you?

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.630
I wish I could say yes.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.500
It was my little sister.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.210
I don't care about the world.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:50.540
The most weight I can bear is two people!

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:52.360
My weak little sister

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:54.210
and our captive princess!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.420
I can't accept that.

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.090
Humanity wouldn't willingly 
choose its own destruction.

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:01.030
That's enough! Stop it, Kuro!

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:05.590
I've had enough of people being 
hurt because of me!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.270
No matter what words you use,

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:12.200
no single life outweighs an entire world!

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:15.840
<i>I'm at a disadvantage against her at range.</i>

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:17.450
<i>So there's only one tactic.</i>

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.790
<i>Close the distance!</i>

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.160
<i>Got her!</i>

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:26.910
No...

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.420
That's not how you use that Card.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.670
<i>What's this?</i>

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:36.920
<i>She teleported just the point?</i>

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:45.060
Yours was the Card I was most wary of, 
but that's all you can do?

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.660
Wha... Il—

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:59.120
Illya!

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.770
No... It can't be...

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:07.040
You idiot! Why would you take my place?!

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.690
Get up, Illya...

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.330
Hey... You're kidding, right?!

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:13.820
Join her.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:18.830
What?

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.280
Huh? Illya?

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:23.050
It's okay, that was...

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.910
Zabaniya.

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:27.700
Assassin's decoy power.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.360
Kuro, listen to me.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:37.270
I just can't agree with your choice.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:38.380
Huh?

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:39.780
Oh?

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:42.920
You... I'm disappointed!

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.520
Is that all Miyu meant to you?

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:46.590
Miyu...

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.610
Miyu is someone I don't want to lose.

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:52.160
She's precious to me.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:53.960
But...

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.840
So are you, Kuro.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:01.930
Just as you worry about me,

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:06.090
there are people I don't want to 
lose, that I won't let go of.

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:09.420
I'm sure everyone in this world feels the same!

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:14.550
So I can't choose.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.860
I can't sacrifice everything

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.470
just for Miyu.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:23.070
<i>Yes, that's the correct answer.</i>

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.580
<i>If there's a chance to save the world,</i>

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.240
<i>individual emotions don't matter.</i>

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:34.300
<i>This has been my fate, ever since 
I was born as the Holy Grail.</i>

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:39.310
<i>These chains of fate will never be broken.</i>

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.880
I can't choose between Miyu and the world.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.570
I'll...

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:49.390
I'll save both Miyu and the world!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:04.290
Saying we have to choose 
is flawed from the start!

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.780
Nonsense.

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:09.260
It's the Holy Grail, right?

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:13.070
We entrust humanity's wishes and 
hopes to the Holy Grail, right?

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.120
So why?

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:18.090
Why aren't we wishing for 
everyone to be happy?!

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:22.330
Illya-sama...

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.000
What the heck?

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:27.050
Do you have a plan when you say that?

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:29.820
I don't know how to make it happen.

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:32.100
But... But...

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:36.350
But...

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.990
Maybe that kind of dream-like wish

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:42.380
is exactly what we should 
entrust to the Holy Grail, right?

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:48.410
Yeah!

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:23.140
I'm touched!

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:26.840
Your willpower has given our princess hope!

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.740
I want you to fight with all your power.

00:23:29.740 --> 00:23:32.760
Try and steal Miyu from me!

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.600
Hope is the very worst poison.

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>To the Princess's Side</b>
